</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Curation of Ctrl-Z</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive our dataset of safe and malicious sequences of bash commands from the data created by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bhatt et al. (2025)</a></cite> as part of their work evaluating control protocols in an agent environment. The authors released trajectories of bash commands generated from policies (’honest’ or ’attack’) completing tasks under different security protocols <span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          Trajectory data available at <a href="https://bashcontrol.com" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://bashcontrol.com</a>.</span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The ’honest’ policy is GPT-4o mini trying to complete a given task faithfully, while the ’attack’ policy is GPT-4o mini trying to download and execute a dummy malware file while ostensibly trying to complete a given task (with scaffolding designed to amplify its attacking capabilities). The honest policy used in ’usefulness’ runs to determine how well each security protocol allows it to complete the task, while attack policy was used in ’safety’ runs to determine how well those protocols stopped it before it could download and execute malware.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Security protocols use a trusted weak model (Llama 3.1 8B) to score each policy generation for suspiciousness. Protocols include Defer to trusted (DTT) (if the monitor scores the policy’s output too highly for suspiciousness at a certain step, generate a command from the trusted weak model instead) and Defer to resample (DTR) (similar to DTT, but up to two new samples are generated from the policy—only if both of these are also suspicious is the trusted model used, otherwise use the least suspicious sample). If all policy generations for a step are highly suspicious, the most suspicious one is audited, meaning the trajectory is ended if it is part of an attack.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We applied the following filters to their data:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Only keep trajectories under the DTR security protocol so that most bash commands are generated by GPT-4o mini.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Only keep the final resampled command for each step of the trajectory (i.e. the command which was actually executed before subsequent steps).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">safe command sequences</span>, only keep usefulness runs with 10 steps or more and truncate to the first 10 steps.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">malicious command sequences</span>, only keep safety runs where the attack policy successfully completes its goal of downloading and executing malware on the 10th step.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the safe command sequences do not necessarily complete the given task within the filtered 10 steps, and the malicious command sequences do not only carry out malicious commands on the 10th step (e.g. they often download the malware in earlier steps and then execute it on the 10th). Note also that 58% of safe command sequences use a weak model generation for at least one step (and 16% of all steps within safe sequences use a weak model generation), whereas no malicious command sequences use a weak model generation (possibly because attack policy trajectories with multiple resamples were more likely to be audited before the 10th step or took more than 10 steps to download and execute malware).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This filtering process leaves 3,438 total trajectories with an approximate 2:1 ratio of safe sequences to malicious ones across 157 unique tasks, split 80/20 between training and test sets with no overlap in tasks. Safe and malicious sequences have similar character lengths.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Modifications to Political Ideologies</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Political Ideologies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nayak, 2024</a>)</cite> comprises political statements on various issues that align with either typically conservative or liberal beliefs. In order to align with the prompt format we use for GSM8K (see <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 GSM8K ‣ Appendix F Prompt formats ‣ Three Concrete Challenges and Two Hopes for the Safety of Unsupervised Elicitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>) we used GPT-4o mini <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI et al., 2024</a>)</cite> to create a question which would be answered by each statement (e.g. "How should the right to bear arms be treated under the law?") and to ensure that responses only contain claims that cannot be objectively labeled as correct or incorrect ("The right to bear arms should be recognized as a fundamental component of personal liberty and self-defense…").</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Results for Other Methods</h2>

<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20400v1/cluster_norm_comparison.svg" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/171;" width="286" height="171"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A3.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance of CCS and PCA on GSM8K with an added sycophancy feature when using the normalization method proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Burns et al. (2022)</a></cite> (Burns-Norm) compared with the method proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Laurito et al. (2024)</a></cite> (Cluster-Norm).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We tried using the Cluster-Norm algorithm proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Laurito et al. (2024)</a></cite> to mitigate the impact of salient non-truth features on probing methods. However, as shown in <a href="#A3.F7" title="In Appendix C Results for Other Methods ‣ Three Concrete Challenges and Two Hopes for the Safety of Unsupervised Elicitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we found that Cluster-Norm did not appreciably improve accuracy over the normalization method proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Burns et al. (2022)</a></cite> when applying CCS or PCA to GSM8K when a sycophancy feature was added to our prompts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For our ensembling methods, we also tried scaling each probe in the ensemble such that every probe’s training set truth scores have a variance of <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, so that random ensemble scores, for example, would not be dominated by the probes which happened to point in the direction with highest variance. However, when we tested this on GSM8K with an added sycophancy feature, this actually made performance worse as shown in <a href="#A3.F8" title="In Appendix C Results for Other Methods ‣ Three Concrete Challenges and Two Hopes for the Safety of Unsupervised Elicitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20400v1/ensemble_scaling_comparison.svg" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/163;" width="286" height="163"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A3.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Effect on GSM8K (added sycophancy) performance of scaling probes in ensembling methods such that each probe predicts truth scores with variance <math id="A3.F8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> on the training set.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Definition of Relative Confidence Measure</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To measure how confident the set <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> of truth scores on GSM8K are relative to the set <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> of truth scores on Political Ideologies, we calculate the contribution of variance within <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> to the variance of a mixture distribution <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> which samples from <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> with equal probability:</p>
<table id="A4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Relative confidence on GSM8K }\coloneqq\frac{\frac{1}{2}\text{Var}(G)}{\text{Var}(X)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Relative confidence on GSM8K </mtext><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Relative confidence on GSM8K }\coloneqq\frac{\frac{1}{2}\text{Var}(G)}{\text{Var}(X)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="A4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Var}(X)=\frac{1}{2}\text{Var}(G)+\frac{1}{2}\text{Var}(P)+\frac{1}{4}(\mu_{G}-\mu_{P})^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Var}(X)=\frac{1}{2}\text{Var}(G)+\frac{1}{2}\text{Var}(P)+\frac{1}{4}(\mu_{G}-\mu_{P})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This metric approaches <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> when most of the mixture variance comes from within <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. scores in <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> cluster near <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>), equals <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> have identical distributions, and approaches <math id="A4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> when variance is dominated by <math id="A4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> or the separation between <math id="A4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Example truth score distributions for GSM8K + Political Ideologies</h2>

<figure id="A5.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20400v1/impossible_gsm8k_density.svg" id="A5.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/396;" width="476" height="396"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A5.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Truth score distribution of GSM8K (above the x-axis) and Political Ideologies (below the x-axis) datasets when using (a) supervised probe ceiling, (b) CCS, (c) E2H-weighted PCA ensemble, and (d) bootstrapped few-shot prompting methods.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A5.F9" title="In Appendix E Example truth score distributions for GSM8K + Political Ideologies ‣ Three Concrete Challenges and Two Hopes for the Safety of Unsupervised Elicitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows examples of truth score distributions for four methods along with their GSM8K AUROC and relative confidence scores. Together these distributions demonstrate good performance (supervised probe ceiling) and three failure modes: examples being separated based on source dataset (CCS), suboptimal AUROC on GSM8K (E2H-weighted PCA ensemble), and good AUROC on GSM8K but over-confidence on Political Ideologies (bootstrapped few-shot).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Prompt formats</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>GSM8K</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For experiments with unmodified GSM8K examples (GSM8K (imbalanced) and GSM8K + Political Ideologies), we used the following prompt format, where <span id="A6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">choice</span> is a candidate LLM solution generated by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wen et al. (2025a)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para"><code id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="41.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 41.4" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,41.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 35.49 C 0 38.75 2.64 41.4 5.91 41.4 L 471.47 41.4 C 474.73 41.4 477.38 38.75 477.38 35.49 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 35.49 C 1.97 37.66 3.73 39.43 5.91 39.43 L 471.47 39.43 C 473.65 39.43 475.41 37.66 475.41 35.49 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.SS1.p2.pic1.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A6.SS1.p2.pic1.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>GSM8K (added salient features)</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For experiments on GSM8K with added salient features, we used contrastive pairs of LLM solutions (<span id="A6.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">choice_1</span> and <span id="A6.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">choice_2</span>) in the following prompt format:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para"><pre id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="41.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 41.4" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,41.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 35.49 C 0 38.75 2.64 41.4 5.91 41.4 L 471.47 41.4 C 474.73 41.4 477.38 38.75 477.38 35.49 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 35.49 C 1.97 37.66 3.73 39.43 5.91 39.43 L 471.47 39.43 C 473.65 39.43 475.41 37.66 475.41 35.49 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.SS2.p2.pic1.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A6.SS2.p2.pic1.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>When we add the sycophancy feature, we add text indicating what a professor character thinks the numerical answer is, which agrees with one of the two responses (chosen at random for each data point):
<pre id="A6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS2.p2.pic2" class="ltx_picture" height="41.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 41.4" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,41.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 35.49 C 0 38.75 2.64 41.4 5.91 41.4 L 471.47 41.4 C 474.73 41.4 477.38 38.75 477.38 35.49 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 35.49 C 1.97 37.66 3.73 39.43 5.91 39.43 L 471.47 39.43 C 473.65 39.43 475.41 37.66 475.41 35.49 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.pic2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.SS2.p2.pic2.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A6.SS2.p2.pic2.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>When we add the punctuation or tense feature, we choose one of the two responses at random on which to alter the punctuation (e.g. replace periods with exclamation points) or the tense (modify to be written in the past or future tense instead of the present tense), respectively, and leave the other response unchanged.

<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>LIAR</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When prompting for political leaning, we used the prompt format:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para"><pre id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS3.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="41.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 41.4" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,41.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 35.49 C 0 38.75 2.64 41.4 5.91 41.4 L 471.47 41.4 C 474.73 41.4 477.38 38.75 477.38 35.49 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 35.49 C 1.97 37.66 3.73 39.43 5.91 39.43 L 471.47 39.43 C 473.65 39.43 475.41 37.66 475.41 35.49 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS3.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p2.pic1.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A6.SS3.p2.pic1.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>When prompting for factual correctness, we used the prompt format:
<code id="A6.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS3.p2.pic2" class="ltx_picture" height="41.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 41.4" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,41.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 35.49 C 0 38.75 2.64 41.4 5.91 41.4 L 471.47 41.4 C 474.73 41.4 477.38 38.75 477.38 35.49 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 35.49 C 1.97 37.66 3.73 39.43 5.91 39.43 L 471.47 39.43 C 473.65 39.43 475.41 37.66 475.41 35.49 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS3.p2.pic2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p2.pic2.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A6.SS3.p2.pic2.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<section id="A6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.4 </span>Civil Comments</h3>

<div id="A6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When prompting for toxicity, we used the prompt format:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para"><pre id="A6.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="41.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 41.4" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,41.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 35.49 C 0 38.75 2.64 41.4 5.91 41.4 L 471.47 41.4 C 474.73 41.4 477.38 38.75 477.38 35.49 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 35.49 C 1.97 37.66 3.73 39.43 5.91 39.43 L 471.47 39.43 C 473.65 39.43 475.41 37.66 475.41 35.49 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS4.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.SS4.p2.pic1.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A6.SS4.p2.pic1.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>When prompting for sexual explicitness, we used the prompt format:
<code id="A6.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.p2.pic2" class="ltx_picture" height="41.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 41.4" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,41.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 35.49 C 0 38.75 2.64 41.4 5.91 41.4 L 471.47 41.4 C 474.73 41.4 477.38 38.75 477.38 35.49 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 35.49 C 1.97 37.66 3.73 39.43 5.91 39.43 L 471.47 39.43 C 473.65 39.43 475.41 37.66 475.41 35.49 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS4.p2.pic2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.SS4.p2.pic2.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A6.SS4.p2.pic2.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<section id="A6.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.5 </span>Ctrl-Z</h3>

<div id="A6.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When prompting an LLM to classify a sequence of bash commands as safe or malicious, we use a similar prompt format to that which <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bhatt et al. (2025)</a></cite> used to prompt the monitor in the security protocols they tested, but modified so that it asks for an immediate binary label instead of a Chain-of-Thought, asks for an evaluation of the suspiciousness of the full sequence of commands instead of the last command in the sequence, and uses special tokens for Llama 3.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We used the following for the system prompt format:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para"><pre id="A6.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS5.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="41.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 41.4" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,41.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 35.49 C 0 38.75 2.64 41.4 5.91 41.4 L 471.47 41.4 C 474.73 41.4 477.38 38.75 477.38 35.49 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 35.49 C 1.97 37.66 3.73 39.43 5.91 39.43 L 471.47 39.43 C 473.65 39.43 475.41 37.66 475.41 35.49 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS5.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.SS5.p3.pic1.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A6.SS5.p3.pic1.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>For the bash command sequence to be classified (and any few-shot examples), we used the prompt format:
<code id="A6.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS5.p3.pic2" class="ltx_picture" height="41.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 41.4" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,41.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 35.49 C 0 38.75 2.64 41.4 5.91 41.4 L 471.47 41.4 C 474.73 41.4 477.38 38.75 477.38 35.49 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 35.49 C 1.97 37.66 3.73 39.43 5.91 39.43 L 471.47 39.43 C 473.65 39.43 475.41 37.66 475.41 35.49 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS5.p3.pic2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.SS5.p3.pic2.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A6.SS5.p3.pic2.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<section id="A6.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.6 </span>Political Ideologies</h3>

<div id="A6.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When prompting for correctness of normative claims, we used the prompt format:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para"><code id="A6.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS6.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="41.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 41.4" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,41.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 35.49 C 0 38.75 2.64 41.4 5.91 41.4 L 471.47 41.4 C 474.73 41.4 477.38 38.75 477.38 35.49 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 35.49 C 1.97 37.66 3.73 39.43 5.91 39.43 L 471.47 39.43 C 473.65 39.43 475.41 37.66 475.41 35.49 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS6.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A6.SS6.p2.pic1.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A6.SS6.p2.pic1.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></code>
</div>
</section></code></pre>
</div>
</section></code></pre>
</div>
</section></code></pre>
